\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Verifier call efficiency as a function of search budget $B$. \textbf  {(a)} Absolute verifier calls: DVA-MCTS is bounded by $N_{\mathcal  {T}}{=}K^D{-}1$ (a constant), saturating well below $O(B)$ for Uniform Verification. In the transition regime ($B \leq N_{\mathcal  {T}}$), empirical counts grow as ${\approx }1.9\sqrt  {B}\log B$. \textbf  {(b)} DVA-MCTS calls as a percentage of Uniform Verification calls, confirming the increasing efficiency advantage at larger budgets (Theorem~\ref {thm:calls}). }}{19}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
